    "description": "# spam-gui\n\nGraphical modules for [spam](https://spam-project.dev) (Software for the Practical Analysis of Materials), in a\n[napari](https://napari.org) viewer. spam-gui is part of the spam project: https://spam-project.dev\n\n- **Multimodal registration** (`spam-gui mmr`): registers two 3D images of the same sample acquired with different\n  modalities (e.g., x-rays and neutrons), step by step, with spam's registration.\n- **Eye registration** (`spam-gui ereg`): as spam's `spam-ereg`, image 1 moved by hand onto image 2, and \u03a6 saved in\n  spam's registration file.\n\nBoth work on large images (several GB, larger than the memory), at several binnings, and share what is done in their\nfirst steps (the images loaded, the eye registration).\n\n## Install\n\n```\npip install spam-gui\n```\n\nin a virtual environment, as spam: a few system libraries first, see\n[INSTALLATION.md](https://gitlab.com/spam-project/spam-gui/-/blob/main/INSTALLATION.md).\n\n## Start\n\n```\nspam-gui                 # the module used last\nspam-gui mmr [image1 image2]\nspam-gui ereg [image1 image2]\nspam-gui --help\n```\n\n## Documentation\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| [INSTALLATION.md](https://gitlab.com/spam-project/spam-gui/-/blob/main/INSTALLATION.md) | Installing, updating; old Qt 5 environments; Linux and Wayland |\n| [USAGE.md](https://gitlab.com/spam-project/spam-gui/-/blob/main/USAGE.md) | Starting it, the modules and their steps, the window, large images |\n| [DEVELOPMENT.md](https://gitlab.com/spam-project/spam-gui/-/blob/main/DEVELOPMENT.md) | Installing to develop, writing a module, tests, releases, the docs website |\n| [SPEC.md](https://gitlab.com/spam-project/spam-gui/-/blob/main/SPEC.md) | How modules are built, how they look and behave (and the specs of each module) |\n\nAll of them, as a website: https://spam-project.gitlab.io/spam-gui/\n\n## Licence\n\nGPL-3.0-or-later, as spam (see [LICENSE.md](https://gitlab.com/spam-project/spam-gui/-/blob/main/LICENSE.md)).\n",
